        "original_id": "914c22a4-8ad1-574d-b1cb-f08d677070e4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Strange Interlude\n- People: Robert Z. Leonard, Norma Shearer, Clark Gable, Eugene O'Neill\n- Companies: Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer\n- Concepts: pre-Code drama films\n- Roles: film actor, military officer\n\nFacts:\n- Strange Interlude is a 1932 American pre-Code drama film.\n- Strange Interlude was directed by Robert Z. Leonard and released by Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer.\n- Strange Interlude stars Norma Shearer and Clark Gable.\n- Strange Interlude is based on the play Strange Interlude by Eugene O'Neill.\n- William Clark Gable was born on February 1, 1901.\n- Clark Gable was an American film actor and military officer.\n- Clark Gable was often called The King of Hollywood or The King.\n- William Clark Gable died on November 16, 1960.",
